  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 3e4b5683c1ea36345958694d590b6436, type: 3}
  m_Name: Q3_PatchPanel
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::QuizQuestionData
  questionText: Besides seating the conductor, what does the punch-down tool do in
    the same stroke?
  choices:
  - Tests continuity on that pair
  - Trims off the excess conductor past the contact
  - Applies a colour label to the port
  - Re-twists the pair behind the contact
  correctChoiceIndex: 1
  points: 10
  explanation: The cutting side of the blade shears the tail as the conductor bottoms
    out. Fit the blade the wrong way round and the tail stays on, ready to short
    against its neighbour.
